# Storage access notes (GCS uses IAM, not a rules file like Firestore)
#
# The bucket itself has NO public access. All access goes through:
#   1. The Cloud Functions runtime service account (roles/storage.objectAdmin)
#   2. Short-lived signed URLs issued by getUploadUrl / getDownloadUrl
#
# The plugin never receives long-lived credentials — only a signed URL
# scoped to one object, valid for ~15 minutes. This is the key security
# property worth calling out in a writeup: the client is never trusted
# with bucket-wide access.
#
# If you outgrow this model (e.g. add real multi-user auth), revisit with:
#   gsutil iam ch <principal>:objectViewer gs://$BUCKET_NAME
# scoped per-user via IAM conditions, rather than broad grants.
